---
number: 329
title: Here Is My Heart!
author: E. Liebich
composer: Unknown
sp_category: "22"
topic: Consecration
---

[verse 1]
Here is my heart! O Lord, I give to Thee
This heart my love, my all.
“Come, leave the world
And give thy heart to me”:
This is to me Thy call.
An offering of love I’m bringing,
With consecrated will I’m singing,
Here is my heart, Here is my heart.

[verse 2]
Here is my heart! Commended to Thy grace,
Though manifold its need;
Take Thou my heart
To be Thy dwelling place;
To Thee my all I cede:
With lust this heart is e’er contending,
So filled with sin, now lowly bending,
Here is my heart, Here is my heart.

[verse 3]
Here is my heart! Surrender full and free,
The cross, it would attain.
It says: “O Lord,
Come be mine all to me,
Thy death shall be my gain.”
Thy wounds, O Saviour, bring salvation,
Eternal peace and consolation
Unto my heart, My faithful heart.
